      "message": "It seems like this call to set the accelerometer back would need to be later in this function.\n\nLet\u0027s say the following happens: \n1. Accelerometer is at 13Hz, like it often is and gyro is at 0.\n\n2. Magnetometer is configured to 100Hz, and this will cause fifo_enable to set the accel register to 100Hz before this function completes\n\n3. Magnetometer is configured to be off.   Since the call to set the magnetometer\u0027s ODR to 0 isn\u0027t until line 528, wouldn\u0027t this call just set the accelerometer to 100Hz again because max_odr is still 100?  And then the fifo_enable call for the magnetometer wouldn\u0027t change the acelerometer because max_odr would now be 13, which isn\u0027t larger than the configured ODR?",
